<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices fall, 13-week flat.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices fall, 13-week flat.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of most Polish T-bills fell at Monday's primary auction on total demand of 867 million zlotys against a 950 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The treasury sold 810 million zlotys of T-bills.  </p>
<p>  T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     95.51    91.16    ---     83.53</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.51)  (91.17)   ---    (83.55)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.56    91.21    ---     83.65</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.57)  (91.22)   ---    (83.63)</p>
<p>   offer		---     200.0    200.0    ---     550.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     139.6    123.5    ---     604.1</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     120.3    101.2    ---     588.6</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     300.0    200.0    ---     700.0</p>
<p>NOTE: Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
